  "description": "<p>This task is to ensure that ghost nodes are immutable. In other words, once a ghost node, always a ghost node.<br/>\n<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bzNvqctv_fzZxDYQFPSfc9_O_9EZl9iJ657dByzaKi0/edit#heading=h.o04fva3x471c\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bzNvqctv_fzZxDYQFPSfc9_O_9EZl9iJ657dByzaKi0/edit#heading=h.o04fva3x471c</a></p>\n\n<p>The following script shows that ghost nodes can currently be re-created as Fedora resources:<br/>\n```<br/>\n#!/usr/bin/bash</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create 'a'<br/>\ncurl -i -XPUT localhost:8080/rest/a</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create 'a/b/c' ('b' is a ghost node)<br/>\ncurl -i -XPUT localhost:8080/rest/a/b/c</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>GET 'a/b' - expect 404<br/>\ncurl -i localhost:8080/rest/a/b</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create 'a/b' - expect 409 &#8211; but no!, it is a 201<br/>\ncurl -i -XPUT localhost:8080/rest/a/b</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>GET 'a/b' - expect 404 &#8211; but, no! it is a 200<br/>\ncurl -i localhost:8080/rest/a/b<br/>\n```</li>\n</ol>\n",
